==== A. Theorem A: harmonic mass of a tree layer = 3^n mu_n(seed) ====
   [A1] Terras classes: for 111 words (n <= 4), a scan of all odd x in (-2^(A+3), 2^(A+3)) finds exactly the 8 elements of ONE residue class mod 2^(A+1), and it is the class (2^A - C_w) 3^-n mod 2^(A+1)  -> VERIFIED [   4.4s]
   [A1b] words of length 5, 6, 8 (900 random words, 6300 tests): every element of the predicted class has the word, no odd element outside it does; failures 0  -> VERIFIED
   [A2] 3000 random odd x (both signs), n <= 12: 3^n x + C_w = 2^A S^n(x) exactly, C_w odd, S^n(x) = Y_n(w) mod 3^n with Y_n(w) = C_w 2^-A = the recursion Y_{k+1} = 2^-a(3Y_k+1)  -> VERIFIED
   [A3] converse: for all words n <= 4, a <= 4, and all odd y in (-4 3^n, 4 3^n), 3 !| y: y = Y_n(w) mod 3^n gives an odd integer x = (2^A y - C_w)/3^n with word w, S^n(x) = y and the sign of y (1360 cases); otherwise x is not an integer (58960 cases)  -> VERIFIED
