==== H. Section 8.1 of the paper: the size of the constants, in iterated logarithms ====
   T* = 10 A* 2^(3E*): log2 T* = 6525.97;  R* = 2^E*(T* + 24586) + 1: log2 R* = 8695.97
   D_exp = 2^(8192 A* 2^(3E*)): log2 log2 D_exp = 6535.6  (the note's 2^(2^6536): correct for D_exp itself)
   D_1 = (128 A* 2^(3E*))^2 + 2: log2 D_1 = 13059;  D_pt = 2(D_1 + L*^2 + 1) + 4 ~ D_1
   P* = g^(R*-1)(T*) with g(t) ~ 10 8^32768 (t+1)^3: R* - 1 ~ 2^8696.0 compositions of a cubic map, so log2 log2 P* ~ (R*-1) log2 3 + 15.8, i.e. log2 log2 log2 P* ~ 8696.63: P* is a tower 2^2^2^8697
   D_sc = 2 + P + P*^10 + 8^32768 (1+P*)^33 + (100 S*)^2 ~ 2^98304 P*^33 >> D_exp; D_bad ~ 2^38 P*; so D* = max(D_1, D_2, D_3) = D_sc, log2 log2 log2 D* ~ 8696.63 (NOT log2 log2 D* ~ 6536)
   C* = (32 A* D*)^A*: log2 C* = A* (5 + log2 A* + log2 D*), so log2 log2 C* ~ 2^8696.63 + 12.6: log2 log2 log2 C* ~ 8696.63 (the note's 'log2 log2 C* ~ 6548' assumed D* = D_exp)
   C = 2 C* 20^6409 + 2 + 2481 ~ C*;  F = 2^467 b^(16b) (C+1) (or 2467 b 16^b (C+1); the extraction is ambiguous, immaterial): log2 F ~ log2 C
   N = 20000 (ceil(log2 F) + 64): log2 N ~ 14.3 + log2 log2 C ~ 2^8696.63: log2 log2 N ~ 8696.63 (the note's 'log2 N ~ 6563' is one exponential short)
   beta(N) ~ 280 (1.01)^N: log2 beta(N) ~ 0.01435 N; q ~ 160 beta(N); M = 4^(2b+1+3q): log2 M ~ 6 q; m ~ M^(1/6);
   c = 3/(256 M^2 m): log2 c^-1 ~ (13/6) log2 M ~ 2080 beta(N), log2 log2 c^-1 ~ 11 + 0.01435 N, log2^(3) c^-1 ~ log2 N - 6.1 ~ 2^8696.63, log2^(4) c^-1 ~ 8696.63: c^-1 is a tower of FOUR twos, 2^2^2^2^8697 (the note's 'beyond 2^(2^(2^6535))' is true but understates by a level)
   J = max(N + N_t, 200(ceil(log2 m) - 78), 2 10^10) ~ 200 log2 m ~ 32000 beta(N) (exponential in N); B = E(J) + ... ~ 42 beta(J), log2 beta(J) ~ 0.01435 J: X_0 = 32(2^B M + 1) has log2^(5) X_0 ~ 8696.63, one level above c^-1 (the note: 'X_0 likewise')
   Lemma 7.3's inequality (7.9): kappa(L+h) + 1 = 7.250120 <= (523/50) L = 7.250320  (margin 1.99e-04)  -> VERIFIED; with 262/25: 7.264182
   3/ln(4/3) = 10.4282; [kappa_0 (L + ln 3) + 1]/L with kappa_0 = 1/ln(4/3): 10.4282 (= 3/ln(4/3): the central-word constant)  -> VERIFIED
   Lemma 4.1: R_0..R_(3^q-1) permute Z/3^q (q <= 4); v_3(R_j - R_k) = v_3(4^(j-k) - 1) - 1 = v_3(j - k) (LTE), so it holds for all q  -> VERIFIED
